cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "strait: Bounds checks for reported summary statistics"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussey
    given-names: Ian
    email: ian.hussey@unibe.ch
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8906-7559"
abstract: >-
  Forensic meta-science tools for checking whether reported summary statistics
  measured on a bounded (truncated) scale are trustworthy. When a measure has a
  known minimum and maximum, the reported mean constrains the standard deviation
  that is arithmetically possible, so the two are not independent. The package
  computes, in closed form, the smallest and largest sample standard deviations
  consistent with a reported mean, sample size and scale range, and flags
  reports that fall outside those bounds as inconsistent.
keywords:
  - meta-science
  - error detection
  - truncated scales
  - summary statistics
  - R
